# TDS 9 (determinism, no host-dependent behavior): artifacts embedded into
# the assemblies and pinned by the frozen grammar lock must check out
# byte-identical on every platform. git's autocrlf rewrites line endings on
# Windows checkouts, which changes the embedded resources, breaks the frozen
# sha256 pins, and — because emitted profiles embed the whole-lock hash
# (develapp.io/grammar-lock-sha256) — breaks cross-platform drift gates.
# Found dogfooding the Minotaur choco lane (windows runner, Minotaur PR #152):
# the lock pinned the LF checkout hashes while the CRLF working-tree files
# hashed differently (exit 5 — first the powershell grammar, then the dotnet
# catalog). Treat lock-pinned artifacts as binary: no conversion, ever.
*.grammar -text
src/SBOBForge.Catalog/catalog/*.json -text
